for actually calling rust from js i made ai give me some helpful notes:

What you need:

- A #[wasm_bindgen] attribute on a public Rust function.
- The function is automatically available as a global in JS with the same name.

Rust side:

#[wasm_bindgen]
pub fn on_reorder(old_index: usize, new_index: usize, value: String) {
    // validate and update your state here
}

JS side:

onEnd: function(evt) {
  window.on_reorder(evt.oldIndex, evt.newIndex, evt.item.querySelector('input').value);
}

That's it. The function name matches. Arguments convert automatically
(numbers, strings, basic types). If your project already compiles to WASM,
wasm_bindgen is already available — just add the attribute and it's callable
from JS.

